WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.444
Week nine.

00:00:01.494 --> 00:00:06.960
Creativity, the last remaining commercial superpower, with creative director Brendan Willenberg.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.704
Commercial creativity is cheating.

00:00:09.754 --> 00:00:11.669
Same inputs as everyone else, but an unfair business advantage.

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:15.879
And it's a method, not a gift.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.705
Step one is solving the real problem.

00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:19.788
Go from the brief,

00:00:19.838 --> 00:00:21.305
past the expected response,

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:22.155
to the real problem,

00:00:21.445 --> 00:00:23.723
then the solution.

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.343
Extra's problem:

00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:27.229
shoppers don't notice gum at the checkout,

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:28.725
because they're on their phones.

00:00:28.775 --> 00:00:32.285
So the Bad Breath Index put a gum prompt into the checkout itself.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.015
Creativity thrives on constraint.

00:00:35.065 --> 00:00:38.620
Rexona couldn't buy media, so it earned it with Pitvertising.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.700
And V called out the whole energy drink category instead of copying Red Bull.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.337
AI can speed-run the process.

00:00:45.387 --> 00:00:48.194
But on its own it gives similar, cheap ideas.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:51.420
Use it as your antagonist, not your assistant.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.110
The takeaway?

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.220
Be simple, not just smart.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:57.825
It's not creative if it's not commercial.
